  "champions-freestyle": `[FREESTYLE] AI DIRECTOR — you are the world's best sports graphic designer and art director. Design the most impressive championship poster you can for this team, completely your own way.

- YOU choose the concept, the scene, the lighting, the colour treatment, the layout and the typography — whatever looks the most powerful and premium for THIS team's crest and colours. Surprise me; don't fall back on a generic template.
- The quality bar: it must look like the official title-winning graphic of a top professional club, finished by a pro design studio — cinematic, photorealistic, bold, clean and expensive. Never cheesy, cluttered, cartoony or "AI-looking".
- Must include: the team crest (faithful to its artwork, never redrawn wrong), a trophy, the title (e.g. "CHAMPIONS"), the team name if given, and the squad names if given (see SQUAD below).
- SQUAD (if given) — NEVER plain text, but NO boxes, plates, tags, frames or bars behind the names: render every name directly on the image in the SAME 3D lettering you chose for the title (same font family, same chrome / gold / metal finish, bevel, reflections, slant and team-colour glow), just smaller, with a hard drop shadow so it pops off the background; arranged in a clean, perfectly aligned grid (2–3 columns) that fits the composition, with sparks, light and confetti around them. Every name the same size, fully readable, spelled exactly. No extra words, labels or numbers.
- NO people, players or faces. Use ONLY the texts given; never invent words, sponsors, websites or handles.`,
  "champions-victory": `[OWN LOOK] VICTORY NIGHT — the moment after the final whistle, captured by a top sports photographer. Clean, powerful, real. NO people, players or faces.

SCENE
- A DARK, cinematic stadium at night shot from pitch level: almost black, swallowed in thick haze and smoke. The TROPHY stands alone on the centre spot, lit by ONE hard white spotlight from directly above — a visible cone of light cutting through the smoke, a bright pool of light on the wet grass, everything outside the beam falling into darkness.
- Behind: only a few huge soft floodlight flares and god-rays high up, a faint silhouette of the stands — NO busy crowd, NO glitter or sparkle bokeh everywhere.
- Ticker-tape kept to a FEW pieces in gold and the team colour, drifting slowly through the light beam with motion blur — never a storm.
- Grade: moody high-contrast, mostly black, white light and silver; only the team colour and the gold accents in colour. Clean negative space so the title and trophy dominate.
- The TROPHY BIG: about 55–60% of the poster height, rising in front of the lower part of the title.
- The TEAM CREST: small at the top centre, AND as a BIG premium 3D metal-and-enamel medallion standing on the grass right NEXT TO the trophy (to one side, slightly behind it, about 85–90% of the trophy height), faithful to the artwork, with real chrome reflections, a team-colour rim light and a soft shadow on the grass.
- BACKGROUND CREST ECHOES: the team crest also appears TWICE as GIANT faded ghosts in the background haze (about 12–18% opacity, slightly blurred, tinted in the team colour), placed diagonally — one in the TOP-LEFT and one in the BOTTOM-RIGHT, each cut off by the edges — like huge projections in the smoke, behind everything.

TYPOGRAPHY
- TITLE (e.g. "CHAMPIONS"): huge clean ultra-condensed white sans-serif capitals (Nike / Adidas campaign style), tight tracking, flat white with a subtle grain — set BEHIND the trophy across the upper half, the trophy overlapping it.
- ECHOES: the same TITLE word repeated THREE more times behind it, stacked downward (or receding into the depth), each one bigger/further back and FADING AWAY — about 35%, then 20%, then 8% opacity — outlined or ghosted white letters dissolving into the crowd bokeh and haze, cut off at the edges. Never competing with the main title.
- Team name: small, wide letter-spaced white capitals above the title. The TEAM CREST small and sharp at the top centre.
- Date (if given): tiny letter-spaced at the bottom.

SQUAD NAMES (if given) — BIG and BAD-ASS, matching the title: the names in the SAME heavy ultra-condensed upright sans-serif as "CHAMPIONS" (bold weight, NOT thin, NOT italic), large — clearly readable from far away — with the same gritty white texture as the title, a slight 3D depth and a hard dark shadow, a cold rim light catching the top edges; set in 2–3 tight, punchy rows at the bottom, names separated by small team-colour slashes ( / ), a thick gold rule above the block and the spotlight haze glowing behind it. Feels like part of the poster's typography, not a caption. Spell every name EXACTLY as written.

REALISM
- A REAL photograph, not an AI image: physically correct light, true reflections on real metal, real smoke and paper, film grain, shallow depth of field. No plastic look, no melted text, no random symbols. The team crest stays faithful to its artwork.

TEXT RULES
- Use ONLY the texts given; spell everything exactly; never invent words, names, sponsors, websites or handles. Write each item once.`,
